x264: do not put extras/ on the include path for QNX 8.0.

extras/ holds MSVC-only shims (its inttypes.h is an #error for other
compilers). Older QNX needed the getopt kept there; QNX 8.0 has a proper
<inttypes.h>, which the shim shadowed. getopt is used only by the CLI, which
is not built.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -746,7 +746,12 @@
         define HAVE_MALLOC_H
         libm="-lm"
         HAVE_GETOPT_LONG=0
-        CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -I\$(SRCPATH)/extras"
+        # extras/ holds MSVC-only shims -- its inttypes.h starts with
+        # #error "Use this header only with Microsoft Visual C++ compilers!".
+        # Older QNX needed the getopt replacement kept there, but QNX 8.0 has a
+        # proper <inttypes.h>/<stdint.h>, so putting extras on the include path
+        # shadows them and the build fails before it starts. getopt is only used
+        # by the CLI, which this port does not build.
         ;;
     *haiku*)
         SYS="HAIKU"
